#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0324-A expect=executionError domain=PC
#expect-execution-error "PCULOQ is declared Char"
#note "R7 (PLAN-column-type-conformance): PCULOQ shipped as Char is nonconformant data. The migrated comparison num(PCORRES) > PCULOQ reads PCULOQ in a numeric order comparison, so per R4 the engine must ERROR rather than silently compare against a text limit. ⚠ Do NOT read the sendig 3-1-1 declaration as a defect: PCULOQ is MODEL-PERMISSIBLE (SDTM model 1.4+) and no SENDIG version enumerates it in PC, which is exactly why this rule exists as its own split half — the PCULOQ dependence is SEND-0324-A's own Executability rather than something dragged into every below-LLOQ finding (R-5.25 split board, issue #219, 2026-09-12). The absent-column case is covered by the -skipped_no_pculoq_column scenario; this one covers the present-but-Char case. Escalation to CDISC to publish the two limits as separate source rows is tracked in the rule-review issue register (internal, not shipped) as issue #219."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetic Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PCSEQ    type=Num
col PCTESTCD type=Char
col PCORRES  type=Char
col PCLLOQ   type=Num
col PCULOQ   type=Char
col PCSTRESC type=Char
---
S1 | PC | 001 | 1 | DRUGX | 250 | 5 | 100 | 250
